WEBVTT

00:00:01.205 --> 00:00:04.696
A Tale of Two Cities by Charles Dickens.

00:00:04.756 --> 00:00:05.527
Chapter 1.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:15.772
Todova.

00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:28.469
It was the year 1775.

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:31.930
A coach was going from London to Dover.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.361
The road was wet and muddy.

00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:38.262
The horses pulled the heavy coach slowly.

00:00:38.322 --> 00:00:42.764
A man on a horse came along the road behind the coach.

00:00:42.824 --> 00:00:44.994
He was riding quickly.

00:00:45.054 --> 00:00:46.725
Stop!

00:00:46.785 --> 00:00:48.726
Shout at the rider.

00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:50.806
What do you want?

00:00:50.866 --> 00:00:53.028
Ask the coach driver.

00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:55.098
I have a message.

00:00:55.158 --> 00:00:57.048
out of the rider.

00:00:57.108 --> 00:01:00.029
He stopped his horse in front of the coach.

00:01:00.089 --> 00:01:02.790
The coach also stopped.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:08.664
The message is for Mr. Jarvis Laurie, said the rider.

00:01:08.724 --> 00:01:12.265
A man looked out of the window of the coach.

00:01:12.325 --> 00:01:17.818
He was about 60 years old, and he wore old-fashioned clothes.

00:01:17.878 --> 00:01:23.776
He saw the rider and asked, what news do you bring, Jerry?

00:01:23.836 --> 00:01:26.764
Do you know this man, sir?"

00:01:26.824 --> 00:01:28.696
asked the coach-driver.

00:01:28.756 --> 00:01:31.338
There are robbers on this road.

00:01:31.398 --> 00:01:33.369
I know him.

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:35.511
Replied the old man.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:38.574
His name is Jerry Cruncher.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.905
He has come from my bank.

00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:45.829
Jerry Cruncher is a messenger, not a robber.

00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:50.848
Here is a letter for you, Mr. Laurie, the messenger said.

00:01:50.908 --> 00:01:56.138
Mr. Telson wants you to wait at the Royal George Inn at Dover.

00:01:56.198 --> 00:02:00.382
A young lady will travel to Paris with you."

00:02:00.442 --> 00:02:02.774
Thank you, Jerry.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.566
Mr. Laurie said.

00:02:04.626 --> 00:02:06.458
He took the letter.

00:02:06.518 --> 00:02:09.140
I will wait in Dover.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:14.308
Good night.

00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:24.760
At the top of the letter were the words, Telson's Bank, Temple Bar, London.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:30.976
The date on the letter was the 18th of November, 1775.

00:02:31.036 --> 00:02:38.462
To Mr. Jarvis Lorry, the letter said, We have news from Telson's Bank in Paris.

00:02:38.522 --> 00:02:41.641
Dr. Manette is alive.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:48.769
He is living at the wine shop of Missia and Madame Defarge in San Antoine, Paris.

00:02:48.828 --> 00:02:51.169
Dr. Manette is ill.

00:02:51.229 --> 00:02:54.350
He was in prison for 18 years.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:03:00.181
Lucy Manette, Dr. Manette's daughter, will meet you in Dover.

00:03:00.241 --> 00:03:03.562
Go to the Royal George Inn in Dover.

00:03:03.622 --> 00:03:06.552
Wait for Lucy Manette there.

00:03:06.612 --> 00:03:09.544
Lucy has never met her father.

00:03:09.604 --> 00:03:12.337
Take Lucy to Paris with you.

00:03:12.397 --> 00:03:17.310
Then bring Dr. Manette and Lucy back to London.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:23.353
The name at the bottom of the letter was Telson.

00:03:23.413 --> 00:03:28.526
Mr. Laurie waited at the Royal George Inn at Dover.

00:03:28.586 --> 00:03:31.858
Miss Lucy Manette arrived the next day.

00:03:31.918 --> 00:03:37.518
She was about 18 years old and she had long golden hair.

00:03:37.578 --> 00:03:41.769
Miss Manet, said Mr. Laurie.

00:03:41.789 --> 00:03:44.050
I work for Telson's Bank.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:50.156
There is a Telson's Bank in London and a Telson's Bank in Paris.

00:03:50.216 --> 00:03:53.698
I often travel between the two cities.

00:03:53.758 --> 00:04:01.845
Twenty years ago, your father came to Telson's Bank in Paris, said Mr. Laurie.

00:04:01.905 --> 00:04:05.488
He left some money in the bank.

00:04:05.547 --> 00:04:07.016
Yes.

00:04:07.076 --> 00:04:08.834
said Lucy Manette.

00:04:08.894 --> 00:04:12.396
My father went to prison, and he died.

00:04:12.456 --> 00:04:15.538
My mother told me about Telson's bank.

00:04:15.598 --> 00:04:18.110
My mother brought me to England.

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:19.511
I was very young.

00:04:19.531 --> 00:04:22.662
I have lived in England all my life.

00:04:22.722 --> 00:04:25.144
But my mother taught me French.

00:04:25.204 --> 00:04:29.707
My mother died a few years ago, Lucy said.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:33.106
And Telson's bank took care of me.

00:04:33.166 --> 00:04:38.046
Your father went to prison, Mr. Laurie said.

00:04:38.106 --> 00:04:40.387
But he did not go to court.

00:04:40.447 --> 00:04:42.388
There was no trial.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.850
That is right, said Lucy.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.631
My father died in prison.

00:04:48.691 --> 00:04:52.973
No, my dear, said Mr. Laurie.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:56.214
I have news of your father.

00:04:56.274 --> 00:04:58.796
He did not die in prison.

00:04:58.856 --> 00:05:03.744
He is alive, and he is living in Paris.

00:05:03.804 --> 00:05:06.462
I will take you to him."

00:05:06.522 --> 00:05:10.324
Lucy Manette put her hand to her face.

00:05:10.384 --> 00:05:12.576
Miss Pross!

00:05:12.636 --> 00:05:14.598
She said loudly.

00:05:14.657 --> 00:05:16.739
Then she fainted.

00:05:16.798 --> 00:05:20.452
She fell into Mr. Laurie's arms.

00:05:20.512 --> 00:05:25.144
A large woman with red hair ran into the room.

00:05:25.204 --> 00:05:27.616
I will take care of her!

00:05:27.676 --> 00:05:28.998
She shouted.

00:05:29.058 --> 00:05:30.698
I am Miss Pross.

00:05:30.758 --> 00:05:39.082
Miss Manette's companion.

00:05:39.142 --> 00:05:56.500
Chapter 2 A Wine Shop in Paris Mr. Laurie, Lucy Manette and Miss Pross went by ship from Dover to Calais.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.182
Then they went by coach to Paris.

00:05:59.242 --> 00:06:03.824
They found the Defarge's wine shop in St Antoine.

00:06:03.884 --> 00:06:09.514
A wooden barrel of wine had broken in the street outside the wine shop.

00:06:09.574 --> 00:06:11.923
People were lying on the ground.

00:06:11.983 --> 00:06:13.743
They were drinking the wine.

00:06:13.803 --> 00:06:16.785
The hands and faces were red.

00:06:16.844 --> 00:06:22.846
Ms. Jafaj, the owner of the wine shop, was standing outside the shop.

00:06:22.906 --> 00:06:26.498
He was watching the people in the street.

00:06:26.558 --> 00:06:33.739
Ms. Jafaj, Mr. Lorry said, My name is Jarvis Lorry.

00:06:33.798 --> 00:06:35.948
This is Miss Manette.

00:06:36.008 --> 00:06:38.448
Where is Doctor Manette?

00:06:38.508 --> 00:06:41.330
We're going to take him to England.

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:45.641
He is ill, said Miss Yudhafaj.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:48.372
My wife is taking care of him.

00:06:48.432 --> 00:06:52.364
Many years ago I was Doctor Manette's servant.

00:06:52.424 --> 00:06:54.364
He helped us then.

00:06:54.424 --> 00:06:56.655
But he went to prison.

00:06:56.715 --> 00:06:59.336
Now we are helping him.

00:06:59.396 --> 00:07:00.686
Come in.

00:07:00.746 --> 00:07:02.826
Come and see him.

00:07:02.886 --> 00:07:10.490
Mr. Lorry, Lucy, Miss Pross, and Missia Defarge went into the wine shop.

00:07:10.549 --> 00:07:13.942
Madame Defarge was sitting in the shop.

00:07:14.002 --> 00:07:16.204
She was knitting with wool.

00:07:16.263 --> 00:07:19.666
Her face was hard and unkind.

00:07:19.726 --> 00:07:24.059
This is Mr. Lorry, said Missia Defarge.

00:07:24.119 --> 00:07:27.081
He wants to see Dr. Manette.

00:07:27.141 --> 00:07:32.677
Dr. Manette will not know you, said Madame Defarge.

00:07:32.736 --> 00:07:35.459
He was in prison for eighteen years.

00:07:35.519 --> 00:07:37.891
He remembers nothing.

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.832
Madam Defarge looked at Lucy.

00:07:40.852 --> 00:07:44.144
"'Are you his daughter?"

00:07:44.203 --> 00:07:45.174
she asked.

00:07:45.194 --> 00:07:48.396
"'Yes,' said Lucy.

00:07:48.416 --> 00:07:50.636
"'I am Lucy Manette.

00:07:50.696 --> 00:07:52.618
I want to see my father.'

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:58.100
"'Come with me,' said Madam Defarge.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:03.941
Madame Defarge took Mr. Laurie and Lucy upstairs to a small room.

00:08:04.001 --> 00:08:06.702
An old man was sitting in the room.

00:08:06.762 --> 00:08:08.813
His hair was white.

00:08:08.873 --> 00:08:11.394
He was making shoes.

00:08:11.454 --> 00:08:14.875
Mr. Laurie spoke to the old man.

00:08:14.935 --> 00:08:18.186
What is your name, Monsieur?

00:08:18.246 --> 00:08:19.847
He asked.

00:08:19.907 --> 00:08:23.148
The old man looked round.

00:08:23.208 --> 00:08:27.872
There is no number 105 North Tower.

00:08:27.932 --> 00:08:30.924
He replied.

00:08:30.984 --> 00:08:35.637
He knows his number in the Bastille prison.

00:08:35.697 --> 00:08:37.958
Said Madame Defarge.

00:08:38.018 --> 00:08:40.890
But he does not know his name.

00:08:40.949 --> 00:08:44.322
Mr. Laurie was a kind man.

00:08:44.382 --> 00:08:47.514
Come with us, Dr. Manette.

00:08:47.574 --> 00:08:49.274
He said quietly.

00:08:49.334 --> 00:08:51.326
Your daughter is here.

00:08:51.386 --> 00:08:54.079
We will take you to England.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:57.194
Dr. Manette did not understand.

00:08:57.254 --> 00:09:00.226
Mr. Laurie held the old man's arm.

00:09:00.286 --> 00:09:02.358
He led him out of the room.

00:09:02.418 --> 00:09:05.210
Dr. Manette walked slowly.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.402
He held a pair of shoes in his hand.

00:09:09.462 --> 00:09:15.956
Mr. Laurie took Dr. Manette, Miss Pross, and Lucy back to England.

00:09:16.016 --> 00:09:19.400
They went by ship from Calais to Dover.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:23.774
On the ship, Dr. Manette was weak and ill.

00:09:23.834 --> 00:09:27.378
A young man helped Lucy and Mr. Laurie.

00:09:27.438 --> 00:09:30.250
They took care of Dr. Manette.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.951
You are kind, sir.

00:09:33.011 --> 00:09:35.512
Lucy said to the young man.

00:09:35.572 --> 00:09:37.713
What is your name?

00:09:37.773 --> 00:09:40.614
My name is Charles Darnay.

00:09:40.674 --> 00:09:42.825
Replied the young man.

00:09:42.885 --> 00:09:44.756
Are you French?

00:09:44.816 --> 00:09:46.316
Asked Lucy.

00:09:46.376 --> 00:09:48.098
Yes, I am.

00:09:48.158 --> 00:09:50.248
Charles Darnay replied.

00:09:50.308 --> 00:09:52.274
But I live in England.

00:09:52.334 --> 00:09:56.052
I often travel between England and France.

00:09:56.112 --> 00:10:04.536
My father has been ill for a long time, said Lucy, but he will get well in England.

00:10:04.596 --> 00:10:08.257
We will meet again, said Darnay.

00:10:08.317 --> 00:10:11.618
I will visit you in England."

00:10:11.678 --> 00:10:16.857
In England, Dr. Manette slowly got well.

00:10:16.917 --> 00:10:20.834
After many months, he started to remember things.

00:10:20.894 --> 00:10:25.076
He remembered his wife, he remembered his daughter.

00:10:25.137 --> 00:10:33.100
But he did not remember the Bastille prison, and he did not remember his journey to England.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:37.942
Lucy and her father lived in a small house in London.

00:10:38.002 --> 00:10:40.023
Miss Pross lived with them.

00:10:40.083 --> 00:10:42.488
She took care of the house.

00:10:42.548 --> 00:10:47.056
Mr. Lorry became a friend of the Manettes and Miss Pross.

00:10:47.116 --> 00:10:49.628
He often visited them.

00:10:49.688 --> 00:10:55.162
One day, Dr. Manette and Lucy received a letter.

00:10:55.222 --> 00:10:58.114
It was a letter from a lawyer.

00:10:58.174 --> 00:11:04.629
You must come to the old Bailey Law Court on Monday, the letter said.

00:11:04.689 --> 00:11:14.670
You must speak at the trial of Charles Darnay.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:28.344
Chapter 3 The Old Bailey Charles Darnay stood in the courtroom.

00:11:28.404 --> 00:11:31.486
He stood in front of the judge and the jury.

00:11:31.546 --> 00:11:37.432
Dr. Manette, Lucy and Mr. Laurie sat at the back of the courtroom.

00:11:37.492 --> 00:11:40.750
A lawyer stood up.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:45.628
The lawyer spoke to the judge and the jury.

00:11:45.688 --> 00:11:51.170
Charles Darnay traveled many times between England and France.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:55.242
The lawyer said, there are some witnesses.

00:11:55.302 --> 00:12:00.074
These people saw Darnay in Dover and in Calais.

00:12:00.134 --> 00:12:05.596
One witness saw Darnay giving some papers to a Frenchman.

00:12:05.656 --> 00:12:08.860
Darnay is a spy.

00:12:08.921 --> 00:12:12.674
The first witness was Lucy Minette.

00:12:12.734 --> 00:12:15.465
Lucy went to the front of the courtroom.

00:12:15.525 --> 00:12:18.646
She answered the lawyer's questions.

00:12:18.706 --> 00:12:22.617
Did you see Charles Darnay on a ship?

00:12:22.677 --> 00:12:24.478
The lawyer asked.

00:12:24.538 --> 00:12:26.168
Yes, I did.

00:12:26.228 --> 00:12:27.809
Lucy replied.

00:12:27.869 --> 00:12:30.600
We were travelling from France to England.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:34.832
Mr. Darnay often travels between England and France.

00:12:34.892 --> 00:12:39.370
Did he speak about the American colonies?

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.406
the lawyer asked?

00:12:41.466 --> 00:12:44.608
No, he did not.

00:12:44.668 --> 00:12:50.322
Then the lawyer asked Dr. Manette and Mr. Lorry the same questions.

00:12:50.382 --> 00:12:54.844
Dr. Manette did not remember his journey from Paris to London.

00:12:54.904 --> 00:12:59.596
Mr. Lorry had not spoken to Charles Darnay.

00:12:59.656 --> 00:13:03.368
Did you see Darnay on the ship?

00:13:03.428 --> 00:13:05.178
The lawyer asked.

00:13:05.238 --> 00:13:08.566
Yes, said Mr. Lorry.

00:13:08.626 --> 00:13:13.874
The next witness was a man with a crooked nose.

00:13:13.935 --> 00:13:17.538
His name was Bassad.

00:13:17.598 --> 00:13:20.340
Mr. Bassad!

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:21.640
The lawyer began.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:25.374
Do you often travel to France?

00:13:25.434 --> 00:13:26.924
Yes, sir.

00:13:26.984 --> 00:13:27.705
I do.

00:13:27.725 --> 00:13:30.578
I answered Bassad.

00:13:30.638 --> 00:13:34.696
Did you see Charles Darnay at Calais?

00:13:34.756 --> 00:13:37.304
Yes, sir, I did.

00:13:37.364 --> 00:13:41.325
I saw him give some papers to a Frenchman.

00:13:41.385 --> 00:13:43.886
Another lawyer stood up.

00:13:43.946 --> 00:13:46.667
He was Charles Darnay's lawyer.

00:13:46.727 --> 00:13:49.968
His name was Stryver.

00:13:50.028 --> 00:13:55.360
Mr. Barsad, what is your business in France?

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:57.620
Mr. Stryver asked.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:00.722
It is private business, sir.

00:14:00.782 --> 00:14:03.028
Barsad answered.

00:14:03.088 --> 00:14:07.978
Do you give letters or papers to Frenchmen sometimes?"

00:14:08.038 --> 00:14:10.280
asked Mr. Stryver.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.242
Yes, sir.

00:14:12.302 --> 00:14:14.504
Bassard replied.

00:14:14.564 --> 00:14:19.338
Charles Darnay also has private business in France.

00:14:19.398 --> 00:14:24.072
Why are his papers different from yours?

00:14:24.132 --> 00:14:28.116
Darnay gave papers to a spy.

00:14:28.176 --> 00:14:30.702
Said Bassard angrily.

00:14:30.762 --> 00:14:33.878
Darnay met the spy at night.

00:14:33.938 --> 00:14:37.749
I heard them speak about George Washington.

00:14:37.809 --> 00:14:43.552
Washington is a revolutionary in the American colonies.

00:14:43.612 --> 00:14:51.434
You saw Darnay and the French spy at night, asked Mr. Stryver.

00:14:51.494 --> 00:14:55.095
Did you see Charles Darnay clearly?

00:14:55.155 --> 00:14:58.846
Yes, sir, replied Bassard.

00:14:58.906 --> 00:15:01.764
I never forget a face.

00:15:01.824 --> 00:15:05.483
Mr. Stryver's clerk was sitting next to him.

00:15:05.543 --> 00:15:08.264
Stryver pointed to this man.

00:15:08.324 --> 00:15:12.487
Mr. Barsad, look at my clerk.

00:15:12.547 --> 00:15:17.110
He said, have you seen this man before?

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:21.672
Everybody in the courtroom looked at Mr. Stryver's clerk.

00:15:21.732 --> 00:15:26.696
The clerk was exactly like Charles Darnay.

00:15:26.756 --> 00:15:31.778
Mr. Barsad did not answer Stryver's question.

00:15:31.838 --> 00:15:39.049
This is my clerk, Mr. Sidney Carton," said Mr. Stryver.

00:15:39.109 --> 00:15:41.840
Is he like Charles Darnay?

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:44.370
Yes.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:48.191
He is, fast-eyed replied.

00:15:48.251 --> 00:15:55.092
Did Mr. Carton give some papers to a French spy in Calais?

00:15:55.152 --> 00:15:57.252
Asked Stryver.

00:15:57.312 --> 00:15:59.323
No, sir.

00:15:59.383 --> 00:16:01.332
It was dark.

00:16:01.392 --> 00:16:02.882
said Stryver.

00:16:02.942 --> 00:16:05.184
You saw a man.

00:16:05.244 --> 00:16:08.155
The man was not Mr. Carton.

00:16:08.215 --> 00:16:11.826
And he was not Charles Darnay.

00:16:11.886 --> 00:16:15.268
Everybody looked at Sidney Carton again.

00:16:15.328 --> 00:16:18.339
He was exactly like Charles Darnay.

00:16:18.399 --> 00:16:20.830
Mr. Stryver was right.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:24.612
The twelve men of the jury left the courtroom.

00:16:24.672 --> 00:16:26.773
They had to make a decision.

00:16:26.833 --> 00:16:29.004
Was Darnay guilty?

00:16:29.064 --> 00:16:32.093
Or was he not guilty?

00:16:32.153 --> 00:16:37.772
A few hours later, the jury came back into the courtroom.

00:16:37.832 --> 00:16:41.044
The judge spoke to one of the jurymen.

00:16:41.104 --> 00:16:43.814
What is your decision?

00:16:43.874 --> 00:16:45.635
He asked.

00:16:45.695 --> 00:16:49.836
Not guilty, said the juryman.

00:16:49.896 --> 00:16:52.147
Darnay is innocent.

00:16:52.207 --> 00:17:02.576
He is not a spy.

00:17:02.636 --> 00:17:17.868
Chapter 4 New Friends Charles Darnay was free.

00:17:17.928 --> 00:17:21.059
He stood outside the old Bailey Law Courts.

00:17:21.119 --> 00:17:23.400
He shook hands with everybody.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:26.731
Dr. Manet looked at Darnay.

00:17:26.792 --> 00:17:29.122
Do I know you?

00:17:29.182 --> 00:17:30.973
Manet asked.

00:17:31.033 --> 00:17:35.435
He helped us on the ship farther, said Lucy.

00:17:35.495 --> 00:17:39.863
But you do not remember our journey to England.

00:17:39.923 --> 00:17:47.234
Charles Darnay and Sidney Carton went to an inn and drank some wine.

00:17:47.294 --> 00:17:50.286
Carton drank a lot of wine.

00:17:50.346 --> 00:17:54.150
You have drunk too much, said Darnay.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:57.426
Do not drink any more, Mr. Carton.

00:17:57.486 --> 00:18:01.934
I always drink too much," said Carton.

00:18:01.994 --> 00:18:04.187
I don't care about people.

00:18:04.247 --> 00:18:06.430
People don't care about me.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:08.971
But I want to drink some wine.

00:18:09.032 --> 00:18:12.274
And I want to think about Miss Lucy Manette.

00:18:12.334 --> 00:18:15.168
She's very beautiful.

00:18:15.228 --> 00:18:19.632
Charles Darnay and Sidney Carton looked at each other.

00:18:19.692 --> 00:18:22.510
They were different in some ways.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:25.426
Darnay was tall and handsome.

00:18:25.486 --> 00:18:29.898
He had smooth dark hair, and he wore fine clothes.

00:18:29.958 --> 00:18:34.701
Cotton had very pale skin and dark eyes.

00:18:34.761 --> 00:18:37.672
His hair and clothes were untidy.

00:18:37.732 --> 00:18:41.224
But the two men were like each other.

00:18:41.284 --> 00:18:47.754
Their faces were the same.

00:18:47.814 --> 00:18:56.610
Four months later, Mr. Jarvis Laurie went to Dr. Manette's house.

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:59.403
The doctor and Lucy were not there.

00:18:59.463 --> 00:19:02.557
Mr. Laurie talked to Miss Pross.

00:19:02.617 --> 00:19:05.410
How is Dr. Manette?

00:19:05.471 --> 00:19:07.165
Asked Mr. Laurie.

00:19:07.225 --> 00:19:11.070
He's well, replied Miss Pross.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:14.614
But sometimes he remembers the Bastille prison.

00:19:14.674 --> 00:19:17.906
Sometimes he walks round and round his room.

00:19:17.966 --> 00:19:20.488
He remembers his work in the prison.

00:19:20.548 --> 00:19:22.600
He makes shoes.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:25.511
Why did he go to prison?

00:19:25.572 --> 00:19:27.182
Asked Laurie.

00:19:27.242 --> 00:19:29.114
Has he told you?

00:19:29.174 --> 00:19:32.317
No, said Miss Pross.

00:19:32.377 --> 00:19:36.550
that a rich and powerful man sent him to the Bastille.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:41.531
In France, powerful aristocrats often send men to prison.

00:19:41.591 --> 00:19:43.902
Rich men make the laws.

00:19:43.962 --> 00:19:47.464
Innocent men go to prison without a trial.

00:19:47.524 --> 00:19:50.154
Yes, said Laurie.

00:19:50.214 --> 00:19:55.486
French aristocrats send men to prison without a trial.

00:19:55.546 --> 00:19:59.414
But now, Dr. Manette's friends help him.

00:19:59.474 --> 00:20:01.050
said Miss Pross.

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:04.112
You are kind to him, Mr. Laurie.

00:20:04.172 --> 00:20:08.974
And Mr. Darnay and Mr. Carton often visit our house.

00:20:09.034 --> 00:20:13.657
I like this house, said Mr. Laurie.

00:20:13.717 --> 00:20:16.378
I do not have a family of my own.

00:20:16.438 --> 00:20:25.072
I visit this house, and I am happy.

00:20:25.132 --> 00:20:34.424
Chapter five, the aristocrat.

00:20:34.484 --> 00:20:37.886
It was a hot day in Paris.

00:20:37.946 --> 00:20:41.218
The Marquis Santevremond was angry.

00:20:41.278 --> 00:20:44.150
He left the palace of the king's minister.

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:47.371
The minister had not spoken to Santevremond.

00:20:47.431 --> 00:20:49.352
The minister was too busy.

00:20:49.412 --> 00:20:51.882
He was drinking chocolate.

00:20:51.942 --> 00:20:54.914
The Marquis got into his coach.

00:20:54.974 --> 00:20:56.855
Go quickly.

00:20:56.875 --> 00:20:59.214
He shouted to the driver.

00:20:59.274 --> 00:21:01.964
Drive to the Shatter.

00:21:02.024 --> 00:21:05.475
The coach went quickly through the streets of Paris.

00:21:05.535 --> 00:21:07.345
People ran away.

00:21:07.405 --> 00:21:09.596
People were afraid of the Marquis.

00:21:09.656 --> 00:21:13.297
They were afraid of the Marquis' coach and horses.

00:21:13.357 --> 00:21:17.498
Suddenly there was a terrible cry.

00:21:17.558 --> 00:21:22.039
The driver stopped the horses at the side of the road.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:24.590
People came out of their houses.

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:27.703
The Marquis shouted to the coach driver.

00:21:27.763 --> 00:21:29.505
What is wrong?

00:21:29.525 --> 00:21:32.446
Mr. The Marquis.

00:21:32.506 --> 00:21:33.907
Said the driver.

00:21:33.967 --> 00:21:36.507
The child ran in front of the coach.

00:21:36.567 --> 00:21:39.278
The horses kicked the child.

00:21:39.338 --> 00:21:41.919
The child is dead.

00:21:41.979 --> 00:21:44.430
Shouted somebody in the crowd.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:46.060
Dead?

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:47.930
Cried a tall man.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.101
Jack!

00:21:49.161 --> 00:21:52.162
My child is dead!

00:21:52.222 --> 00:21:55.792
Who is the father of the child?

00:21:55.852 --> 00:21:57.699
Shouted the Marquis.

00:21:57.759 --> 00:22:01.476
It is Gaspar, said a voice.

00:22:01.536 --> 00:22:05.268
Gaspar, shouted the Marquis.

00:22:05.328 --> 00:22:09.190
Here is some money."

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:15.048
The Marquis threw a gold coin out of the window of the coach.

00:22:15.108 --> 00:22:48.097
nobody moved nobody picked up the coin everybody was afraid of the marquee they were afraid of rich and powerful aristocrats then somebody threw the gold coin back into the coach the aristocrat looked at the crowd of people he hated them he spoke to the coach driver drive to the shadow he said The coach moved away from the crowd.

00:22:48.157 --> 00:22:51.590
The Marquis forgot about the dead child.

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:59.086
A man ran after the coach, but the Marquis did not see him.

00:22:59.146 --> 00:23:05.181
In the evening, the coach arrived at the Chateau of St. everyone.

00:23:05.241 --> 00:23:09.804
Gabel, an old servant, was waiting for the Marquis.

00:23:09.865 --> 00:23:13.676
Mr. the Marquis, said Gabel.

00:23:13.736 --> 00:23:16.186
I was watching your coach.

00:23:16.246 --> 00:23:20.418
A man was holding on to the back of the coach.

00:23:20.479 --> 00:23:22.039
A man?

00:23:22.099 --> 00:23:23.930
Where is he?"

00:23:23.990 --> 00:23:25.782
asked the Marquis.

00:23:25.842 --> 00:23:29.594
He jumped into the bushes beside the road.

00:23:29.654 --> 00:23:35.976
Replied Gabel, thanked him quickly, shouted the aristocrat.

00:23:36.036 --> 00:23:40.079
Now, has Missier Charles arrived?

00:23:40.139 --> 00:23:42.224
Has he come from England?

00:23:42.284 --> 00:23:45.018
No, Mr. The Marquis."

00:23:45.078 --> 00:23:47.629
Gabel replied.

00:23:47.689 --> 00:23:52.620
Later in the evening, the Marquis was in his dining-room.

00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:54.920
He was eating his supper.

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:57.591
He looked out of the window.

00:23:57.651 --> 00:24:00.431
He saw a man outside.

00:24:00.451 --> 00:24:03.192
"'Gabel?"

00:24:03.252 --> 00:24:05.112
shouted the Marquis loudly.

00:24:05.132 --> 00:24:08.163
"'There is a man outside the shadow.

00:24:08.223 --> 00:24:09.833
Who is he?'

00:24:09.893 --> 00:24:12.644
Gabel looked out of the window.

00:24:12.704 --> 00:24:14.894
The night was dark.

00:24:14.954 --> 00:24:19.346
There is nobody outside, Mr. The Marquis.

00:24:19.406 --> 00:24:21.476
The servant said.

00:24:21.536 --> 00:24:24.138
Then Gabel listened.

00:24:24.198 --> 00:24:26.878
But I can hear something.

00:24:26.938 --> 00:24:28.379
He said.

00:24:28.439 --> 00:24:31.300
I can hear a coach.

00:24:31.360 --> 00:24:32.890
Good.

00:24:32.950 --> 00:24:36.041
My nephew Charles has arrived.

00:24:36.102 --> 00:24:38.680
Said the Marquis.

00:24:38.740 --> 00:24:46.340
A few minutes later, Charles Darnay came into the dining room.

00:24:46.400 --> 00:24:49.722
Good evening, Uncle.

00:24:49.782 --> 00:24:51.152
He said.

00:24:51.212 --> 00:24:53.694
Good evening, Charles.

00:24:53.754 --> 00:24:55.324
Said the Marquis.

00:24:55.384 --> 00:24:59.126
How is your life in England?

00:24:59.186 --> 00:25:01.618
My life is good, Uncle.

00:25:01.678 --> 00:25:03.889
Replied Charles Darnay.

00:25:03.949 --> 00:25:07.811
Why do you live in England?

00:25:07.871 --> 00:25:09.372
Said the Marquis.

00:25:09.433 --> 00:25:12.165
You must come back to France.

00:25:12.225 --> 00:25:15.138
Soon I will die.

00:25:15.198 --> 00:25:19.390
Then you will be the Marquis at Everimond.

00:25:19.451 --> 00:25:23.824
I do not want to be a Marquis," said Darnay.

00:25:23.884 --> 00:25:27.116
I do not use the name, Santa Everimond.

00:25:27.176 --> 00:25:30.439
I do not want to be an aristocrat.

00:25:30.499 --> 00:25:32.862
Nonsense!

00:25:32.922 --> 00:25:35.051
said the Marquis angrily.

00:25:35.111 --> 00:25:37.760
You are an aristocrat.

00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:40.640
We shall talk about this tomorrow."

00:25:40.701 --> 00:25:44.052
I do not want to talk about this, Uncle.

00:25:44.112 --> 00:25:45.752
Darno replied.

00:25:45.812 --> 00:25:49.183
I will return to England early in the morning.

00:25:49.243 --> 00:25:52.234
Good night.

00:25:52.294 --> 00:25:56.756
The Marquis went to bed.

00:25:56.816 --> 00:26:00.357
He remembered the dead child in Paris.

00:26:00.417 --> 00:26:02.798
He remembered the tall man.

00:26:02.858 --> 00:26:05.085
The man had cried out.

00:26:05.145 --> 00:26:06.563
Dead!

00:26:06.623 --> 00:26:09.236
My child is dead!"

00:26:09.296 --> 00:26:13.180
Gabel had seen a man holding onto his coach.

00:26:13.240 --> 00:26:15.654
The Marquis remembered that.

00:26:15.714 --> 00:26:20.228
He himself had seen a man outside the window of the chateau.

00:26:20.288 --> 00:26:22.642
He remembered that.

00:26:22.702 --> 00:26:27.318
Suddenly, the Marquis was afraid.

00:26:27.378 --> 00:26:31.722
Charles Darnay left the chateau early in the morning.

00:26:31.782 --> 00:26:33.924
He did not speak to his uncle.

00:26:33.984 --> 00:26:36.536
He did not want to speak to his uncle.

00:26:36.596 --> 00:26:40.430
And Charles could not speak to him.

00:26:40.490 --> 00:26:44.552
The Marquis Antebrymond was dead.

00:26:44.612 --> 00:26:56.217
He lay in his bed, and knife was in his chest.

00:26:56.277 --> 00:27:12.759
Chapter 6 A Wedding One day in the summer Charles Darnay visited Dr. Manette at his house in London.

00:27:12.819 --> 00:27:18.650
Sir, he said, I am a teacher and a translator.

00:27:18.711 --> 00:27:22.562
I am a Frenchman, but I live in England.

00:27:22.622 --> 00:27:25.772
Life in France is too difficult.

00:27:25.832 --> 00:27:29.972
Yes, yes, Sir Dr. Manette.

00:27:30.032 --> 00:27:33.044
There is only bad news from France.

00:27:33.064 --> 00:27:38.129
"'I have often visited your house,' said Darnay.

00:27:38.149 --> 00:27:41.072
"'You are a kind man and a good doctor.

00:27:41.092 --> 00:27:44.475
"'And I am in love with your daughter.

00:27:44.495 --> 00:27:49.030
"'Sir, I want to marry Lucy.'

00:27:49.090 --> 00:27:51.342
Dr. Manette was surprised.

00:27:51.362 --> 00:27:54.654
"'Does Lucy know this?'

00:27:54.714 --> 00:27:56.224
he asked.

00:27:56.284 --> 00:27:58.564
No, replied Darnay.

00:27:58.625 --> 00:28:00.726
I will ask her today.

00:28:00.786 --> 00:28:04.638
Sir, will you let me marry Lucy?

00:28:04.699 --> 00:28:08.262
Yes, said Doctor Manette.

00:28:08.322 --> 00:28:13.766
Please, speak to her.

00:28:13.826 --> 00:28:22.221
A few days later, Monsieur Defarge was in his wine shop in Paris.

00:28:22.282 --> 00:28:24.548
He had some news.

00:28:24.608 --> 00:28:27.426
Gaspar is dead.

00:28:27.486 --> 00:28:29.667
Defarge said to his wife.

00:28:29.727 --> 00:28:31.708
He went to the guillotine.

00:28:31.768 --> 00:28:34.310
He died today.

00:28:34.370 --> 00:28:38.262
Gaspar killed the Marquisant Everimond.

00:28:38.322 --> 00:28:40.404
Said Madame Defarge.

00:28:40.464 --> 00:28:43.576
But the people have suffered too much.

00:28:43.636 --> 00:28:47.178
The cruel aristocrats made the old laws.

00:28:47.239 --> 00:28:50.590
Now the people must make new laws.

00:28:50.650 --> 00:28:55.634
Soon we will kill all the aristocrats.

00:28:55.694 --> 00:28:58.934
Be careful!"

00:28:58.994 --> 00:29:01.266
said Missia de Farge quickly.

00:29:01.326 --> 00:29:03.406
Those are dangerous words.

00:29:03.466 --> 00:29:06.277
There is a stranger in Santa Antoine.

00:29:06.337 --> 00:29:10.259
He speaks French well, but he is English.

00:29:10.319 --> 00:29:12.200
He is a spy.

00:29:12.260 --> 00:29:15.970
His name is Basad.

00:29:16.030 --> 00:29:21.492
At that moment, Basad himself came into the shop.

00:29:21.552 --> 00:29:25.358
Good afternoon, he said.

00:29:25.418 --> 00:29:29.213
The news about Gaspar is bad.

00:29:29.273 --> 00:29:32.223
He killed the Marquis Aunt every month.

00:29:32.283 --> 00:29:34.684
Said Madame Defarge carefully.

00:29:34.744 --> 00:29:37.484
And now he is dead.

00:29:37.544 --> 00:29:41.445
Why did Gaspar kill the Marquis?

00:29:41.505 --> 00:29:43.635
asked Bar Sad.

00:29:43.696 --> 00:29:46.446
Gaspar was a bad man.

00:29:46.506 --> 00:29:48.547
He was executed.

00:29:48.607 --> 00:29:50.928
Said Monsieur Defarge.

00:29:50.988 --> 00:29:54.921
Was the Marquis a bad man, too?

00:29:54.981 --> 00:29:58.192
Was he executed, too?"

00:29:58.252 --> 00:30:00.132
asked Bassad.

00:30:00.192 --> 00:30:02.793
We know nothing about that!

00:30:02.853 --> 00:30:05.644
Miss Yudafaj said quickly.

00:30:05.704 --> 00:30:09.215
Bassad bought a glass of wine.

00:30:09.275 --> 00:30:14.846
There is a new Marquis and every man, he said.

00:30:14.906 --> 00:30:19.308
Yes, he is the nephew of the old Marquis.

00:30:19.368 --> 00:30:21.977
Replied Madame Befarge.

00:30:22.037 --> 00:30:24.177
The nephew!

00:30:24.237 --> 00:30:25.808
Charles!

00:30:25.868 --> 00:30:28.290
He lives in England!"

00:30:28.350 --> 00:30:31.242
Bassad said slowly.

00:30:31.302 --> 00:30:34.755
He looked at Madame Defarge.

00:30:34.815 --> 00:30:37.306
Does he live in England?

00:30:37.366 --> 00:30:39.718
said Madame Defarge.

00:30:39.778 --> 00:30:42.590
She did not look at Bassad.

00:30:42.651 --> 00:30:44.662
I know about you!

00:30:44.682 --> 00:30:46.908
said Bassad.

00:30:46.968 --> 00:30:50.903
Dr. Manette came out of the Bastille prison.

00:30:50.963 --> 00:30:53.073
You took care of him.

00:30:53.133 --> 00:30:55.204
Is that true?"

00:30:55.264 --> 00:30:59.515
Everybody knows that, said Madame Defarge.

00:30:59.575 --> 00:31:03.316
Many years ago, my husband was the doctor's servant.

00:31:03.376 --> 00:31:06.186
The doctor helped my family.

00:31:06.246 --> 00:31:10.378
Why did Dr. Manette go to prison?

00:31:10.438 --> 00:31:12.408
asked Barsad.

00:31:12.468 --> 00:31:16.574
Did Sant'Everemond send him to the Bastille?

00:31:16.634 --> 00:31:20.551
"'We do not know, monsieur,' said Madame Defarge.

00:31:20.571 --> 00:31:23.173
"'You must not speak about this.'

00:31:23.193 --> 00:31:27.356
"'Very well,' said Basad.

00:31:27.376 --> 00:31:30.539
"'But I can tell you some news.

00:31:30.559 --> 00:31:35.663
"'Dr. Manette's daughter, Lucy, is going to get married.

00:31:35.683 --> 00:31:38.145
"'She will be married in London.

00:31:38.165 --> 00:31:43.169
"'In England, her husband is called Charles Darnay.

00:31:43.189 --> 00:31:47.154
"'But in France he has another name.

00:31:47.214 --> 00:31:55.941
He is Charles, Monsieur the Marquis and Evermind.

00:31:56.001 --> 00:32:04.808
Once Sunny Day in London, Charles Darnay married Lucy Manette.

00:32:04.868 --> 00:32:09.441
Mr Jarvis Laurie and Mr Sydney Carton came to the wedding.

00:32:09.501 --> 00:32:11.752
It was a happy day.

00:32:11.812 --> 00:32:15.526
But Sydney Carton was not very happy.

00:32:15.586 --> 00:32:18.350
He shook Charles Darnay's hand.

00:32:18.410 --> 00:32:20.812
He kissed Lucy.

00:32:20.873 --> 00:32:25.426
You are my good friends, he said.

00:32:25.486 --> 00:32:28.200
I do not have many friends.

00:32:28.260 --> 00:32:30.732
Now you are married.

00:32:30.792 --> 00:32:34.436
Please let me visit your new house sometimes.

00:32:34.496 --> 00:32:38.640
You will be welcome, said Darnay.

00:32:38.700 --> 00:32:44.665
We will always be your friends.

00:32:44.725 --> 00:33:03.376
Chapter 7 Revolution Several years passed.

00:33:03.436 --> 00:33:15.104
Charles and Lucy Darnay had a daughter.

00:33:15.164 --> 00:33:18.796
They called the girl Lucy, like a mother.

00:33:18.856 --> 00:33:23.678
Sidney Carton and Jarvis Laurie often visited the family.

00:33:23.739 --> 00:33:30.352
One night, in July 1789, Mr. Laurie visited the house.

00:33:30.412 --> 00:33:35.105
I have come from Towson's bank, said Mr. Laurie.

00:33:35.165 --> 00:33:37.116
There was a lot of work today.

00:33:37.136 --> 00:33:39.647
I have news from Paris.

00:33:39.707 --> 00:33:41.757
It is not good news.

00:33:41.817 --> 00:33:47.371
The people are fighting in the streets of Paris," said Mr. Laurie.

00:33:47.431 --> 00:33:49.992
They have opened the Bastille prison.

00:33:50.052 --> 00:33:52.204
All the prisoners are free.

00:33:52.264 --> 00:33:56.277
There is a revolution in France, Mr. Laurie said.

00:33:56.337 --> 00:33:58.528
The people want a republic.

00:33:58.588 --> 00:34:00.350
They do not want a king.

00:34:00.410 --> 00:34:05.293
The people want a new government, but they do not want the aristocrats.

00:34:05.353 --> 00:34:11.325
There are many trials and many executions in Paris," the banker said.

00:34:11.385 --> 00:34:14.266
The people watched the executions.

00:34:14.326 --> 00:34:17.337
The guillotine cuts off many heads.

00:34:17.397 --> 00:34:20.458
It cuts off the heads of the aristocrats.

00:34:20.518 --> 00:34:23.799
Each time an aristocrat dies.

00:34:23.859 --> 00:34:27.580
Said Mr. Laurie, the people are happy.

00:34:27.640 --> 00:34:30.371
Death to all aristocrats!

00:34:30.431 --> 00:34:31.402
They shout!

00:34:31.462 --> 00:34:33.683
Long live the Republic!

00:34:33.743 --> 00:34:37.474
Long live the revolution!

00:34:37.535 --> 00:34:43.808
Outside the shadow of St. Everimond, the people were very angry.

00:34:43.868 --> 00:34:46.388
Kill all the aristocrats!

00:34:46.448 --> 00:34:48.360
Burn the shadow!

00:34:48.420 --> 00:34:50.148
They shouted.

00:34:50.208 --> 00:34:54.767
The servants Gabel wanted to save the Chateau.

00:34:54.827 --> 00:34:56.558
But nobody helped him.

00:34:56.618 --> 00:34:58.749
The people lit fires.

00:34:58.809 --> 00:35:02.651
The Chateau burned to the ground.

00:35:02.711 --> 00:35:07.833
The people wanted to kill the Marquis Aunt Everimand.

00:35:07.894 --> 00:35:10.385
But they could not find the Marquis.

00:35:10.445 --> 00:35:12.926
The old Marquis was dead.

00:35:12.986 --> 00:35:16.448
The new Marquis never came to France.

00:35:16.508 --> 00:35:20.605
The people sent Gabel to prison.

00:35:20.665 --> 00:35:23.041
Where is the Marquis?

00:35:23.101 --> 00:35:24.462
They asked him.

00:35:24.522 --> 00:35:31.126
Only the Marquis can save you.

00:35:31.186 --> 00:35:39.581
In the next months, many French aristocrats came to London.

00:35:39.641 --> 00:35:42.282
They brought news from Paris.

00:35:42.342 --> 00:35:46.736
Charles Darnay was now the Marquis and Everimond.

00:35:46.796 --> 00:35:49.357
But he did not tell anybody.

00:35:49.417 --> 00:35:51.614
It was a secret.

00:35:51.674 --> 00:35:56.522
One day Charles received a letter from France.

00:35:56.582 --> 00:36:04.047
At the top of the letter were the words, Prison of the Abbei, Paris.

00:36:04.108 --> 00:36:08.740
To miss your Charles, the Marquis Saint-Everymont.

00:36:08.800 --> 00:36:12.172
The letter said, Please help me.

00:36:12.192 --> 00:36:14.374
I am in prison.

00:36:14.434 --> 00:36:17.266
I was the servant of your family.

00:36:17.326 --> 00:36:19.586
Soon I will die.

00:36:19.647 --> 00:36:21.860
Please come to Paris.

00:36:21.920 --> 00:36:23.894
Please help me.

00:36:23.955 --> 00:36:31.862
Your family servant, Teirfield Gabel.

00:36:31.922 --> 00:36:37.508
Chapter 8.

00:36:37.568 --> 00:36:43.784
To Paris.

00:36:43.844 --> 00:36:50.771
Charles Darnay spoke to Mr. Lorry.

00:36:50.791 --> 00:36:54.013
"'I must go to Paris,' he said.

00:36:54.033 --> 00:36:56.455
"'I must help a servant of my family.'

00:36:56.475 --> 00:36:58.707
"'Paris?'

00:36:58.767 --> 00:37:00.508
said Mr. Lorry.

00:37:00.569 --> 00:37:02.860
"'Dr. Manette will be very worried.

00:37:02.880 --> 00:37:05.262
"'Your family will be very worried.'

00:37:05.282 --> 00:37:09.426
"'Please do not tell my family today,' said Darnay.

00:37:09.446 --> 00:37:11.107
"'Tell them tomorrow.

00:37:11.127 --> 00:37:16.714
"'Tomorrow I will be in Paris, and soon I will be back in London.

00:37:16.774 --> 00:37:20.720
Very well, said Mr. Laurie.

00:37:20.780 --> 00:37:23.761
I too must go to Paris soon.

00:37:23.821 --> 00:37:27.424
I must get some papers from Telson's bank in Paris.

00:37:27.484 --> 00:37:29.735
I must bring them back to London.

00:37:29.795 --> 00:37:32.466
Paris is very dangerous now.

00:37:32.527 --> 00:37:35.738
The revolution has made people wild.

00:37:35.798 --> 00:37:40.622
Then I will send a message to you at Telson's bank, said Darnay.

00:37:40.682 --> 00:37:43.604
I will meet you in Paris.

00:37:43.664 --> 00:37:48.727
Charles Darnay went by ship from Dover to Calais.

00:37:48.787 --> 00:37:51.949
Many things in France had changed.

00:37:52.009 --> 00:37:55.880
There were many revolutionary guards in every town.

00:37:55.940 --> 00:38:00.934
French people no longer called each other Monsieur or Madame.

00:38:00.994 --> 00:38:05.896
Everybody had to be called Citizen or Citizen S.

00:38:05.956 --> 00:38:09.658
Everybody was equal in the New Republic.

00:38:09.718 --> 00:38:11.819
There were no aristocrats.

00:38:11.879 --> 00:38:15.912
There was no king.

00:38:15.973 --> 00:38:21.266
Charles went from Calais by coach.

00:38:21.326 --> 00:38:25.078
Outside the town, the coach stopped.

00:38:25.138 --> 00:38:29.030
Revolutionary guards were standing in the road.

00:38:29.090 --> 00:38:31.641
Who are you, citizen?

00:38:31.701 --> 00:38:34.532
One of the Revolutionary guards asked.

00:38:34.592 --> 00:38:38.454
Show us your papers, said another guard.

00:38:38.514 --> 00:38:40.465
Do you have a travel permit?

00:38:40.525 --> 00:38:43.276
What is your business in France?

00:38:43.336 --> 00:38:47.520
I'm going to Paris, said Darnay.

00:38:47.580 --> 00:38:50.123
Please let me go on.

00:38:50.184 --> 00:38:55.487
This man is an aristocrat, said the first guard.

00:38:55.548 --> 00:38:58.680
He left France and he went to England.

00:38:58.740 --> 00:39:01.451
He must go to the guillotine.

00:39:01.512 --> 00:39:06.496
I'm going to Paris on business, Darnay said.

00:39:06.556 --> 00:39:12.470
Yes, you are going to Paris, said the second guard.

00:39:12.530 --> 00:39:14.422
You are going to prison.

00:39:14.482 --> 00:39:16.826
You are under arrest.

00:39:16.886 --> 00:39:19.058
Why am I under arrest?"

00:39:19.118 --> 00:39:21.219
asked Darnay angrily.

00:39:21.279 --> 00:39:25.740
You are an aristocrat, said the first guard.

00:39:25.801 --> 00:39:30.652
All aristocrats are enemies of the revolution and enemies of the Republic.

00:39:30.712 --> 00:39:33.913
All aristocrats are enemies of the people.

00:39:33.973 --> 00:39:36.074
The guillotine is waiting.

00:39:36.134 --> 00:39:39.624
It is waiting for you.

00:39:39.684 --> 00:39:44.036
A crowd of people stood around the coach.

00:39:44.096 --> 00:39:46.678
Death to all aristocrats.

00:39:46.739 --> 00:39:52.412
They shouted, take him to Paris.

00:39:52.472 --> 00:39:58.476
The Revolutionary Guards took Darnay to Paris.

00:39:58.536 --> 00:40:03.128
They put him in La Force prison.

00:40:03.188 --> 00:40:08.010
They found the letter from Gabel in his coat.

00:40:08.070 --> 00:40:12.722
This is a letter to Santa everymond, said a guard.

00:40:12.782 --> 00:40:14.283
We know that name.

00:40:14.343 --> 00:40:17.138
The people hate that name.

00:40:17.198 --> 00:40:21.494
The next day, a man visited Charles.

00:40:21.554 --> 00:40:24.516
The man was a revolutionary official.

00:40:24.576 --> 00:40:27.217
He looked at Darnay.

00:40:27.278 --> 00:40:31.190
I know your face, he said.

00:40:31.250 --> 00:40:33.722
You were sons every month.

00:40:33.782 --> 00:40:36.774
I am Citizen Defarge.

00:40:36.834 --> 00:40:40.136
Mr. Defarge, said Darnay.

00:40:40.196 --> 00:40:41.976
I know your name.

00:40:42.036 --> 00:40:44.558
You helped Dr. Manette.

00:40:44.618 --> 00:40:47.320
You must call me Citizen.

00:40:47.380 --> 00:40:49.430
We are all equal now.

00:40:49.491 --> 00:40:52.982
There are no more misjures and Marquesas.

00:40:53.042 --> 00:40:58.064
Citizen Defarge, will you take a message to Telson's bank?

00:40:58.124 --> 00:40:59.644
Ask Darnay.

00:40:59.704 --> 00:41:02.455
It is a message for Mr. Lorry.

00:41:02.515 --> 00:41:05.526
He will give the message to Dr. Manet.

00:41:05.586 --> 00:41:10.408
I will not take your message, said Defarge.

00:41:10.468 --> 00:41:12.528
You were an aristocrat.

00:41:12.589 --> 00:41:16.040
You are an enemy of the Republic."

00:41:16.100 --> 00:41:18.372
What will happen to me?

00:41:18.433 --> 00:41:20.194
asked Darnay.

00:41:20.254 --> 00:41:24.267
There will be a trial in the people's court.

00:41:24.327 --> 00:41:35.799
Then you will go to the guillotine, said Defarge.

00:41:35.860 --> 00:41:51.226
CHAPTER IX AN ENEMY OF THE REPUBLIC Mr. Laurie was at Telson's Bank in Paris.

00:41:51.286 --> 00:41:53.478
He got some news.

00:41:53.538 --> 00:41:55.540
It was bad news.

00:41:55.600 --> 00:41:59.603
Charles Darnay was in La Force Prison.

00:41:59.664 --> 00:42:03.326
Immediately Mr. Laurie sent a message to London.

00:42:03.386 --> 00:42:05.518
He sent it to Dr. Manette.

00:42:05.578 --> 00:42:09.762
Dr. Manette came to Paris with Lucy and her child.

00:42:09.822 --> 00:42:13.635
Miss Pross and Jerry Cruncher came too.

00:42:13.695 --> 00:42:17.106
They stayed in rooms near the bank.

00:42:17.167 --> 00:42:21.158
Dr. Manette spoke to Mr. Laurie.

00:42:21.218 --> 00:42:27.612
I was a prisoner in the Bastille prison for eighteen years, he said.

00:42:27.672 --> 00:42:30.354
The revolutionaries will listen to me.

00:42:30.414 --> 00:42:36.687
I will speak at Charles's trial, and I will speak to Miss Year and Madame Defarge.

00:42:36.747 --> 00:42:38.674
They will help us.

00:42:38.734 --> 00:42:43.250
I will speak to Madame Defarge too," said Lucy.

00:42:43.310 --> 00:42:46.470
I am a wife, and I am a mother.

00:42:46.530 --> 00:42:50.442
Madame Defarge will understand she will help us.

00:42:50.502 --> 00:42:54.542
Lucy went to the wine shop in Santa Antoine.

00:42:54.602 --> 00:43:01.063
She spoke to Madame Defarge, but Madame Defarge would not help her.

00:43:01.124 --> 00:43:05.455
Your husband is an aristocrat, she said.

00:43:05.515 --> 00:43:07.496
Now he is in prison.

00:43:07.556 --> 00:43:12.331
Before the revolution, the aristocrats sent poor people to prison.

00:43:12.391 --> 00:43:14.282
We were helpless.

00:43:14.342 --> 00:43:18.775
Now all that is finished," Madam Defarge said.

00:43:18.835 --> 00:43:21.587
The aristocrats have finished too.

00:43:21.647 --> 00:43:24.819
Your husband's trial will be tomorrow.

00:43:24.879 --> 00:43:27.971
I cannot help you.

00:43:28.031 --> 00:43:34.868
Charles Santevremond, also called Charles Darnay.

00:43:34.928 --> 00:43:38.532
The President of the Court shouted the name.

00:43:38.592 --> 00:43:40.734
Charles Darnay stood up.

00:43:40.794 --> 00:43:43.206
He stood in front of the judges.

00:43:43.266 --> 00:43:45.096
He answered their questions.

00:43:45.116 --> 00:43:51.521
"'You are an aristocrat and an enemy of the Republic,' said the President.

00:43:51.541 --> 00:43:54.563
"'No,' answered Darnay.

00:43:54.583 --> 00:43:57.746
"'I do not live in France.

00:43:57.806 --> 00:44:00.878
I have not treated the French people badly.

00:44:00.938 --> 00:44:03.942
I did not take money from the people.

00:44:04.002 --> 00:44:07.576
I do not want to be the Marquis Antebremand."

00:44:07.636 --> 00:44:09.987
Are there witnesses?

00:44:10.047 --> 00:44:11.808
asked the President.

00:44:11.868 --> 00:44:14.640
Will somebody speak for you?

00:44:14.700 --> 00:44:16.300
Yes.

00:44:16.360 --> 00:44:23.824
Citizen Teofield Gabel and Dr. Alexandra Manette will speak for me, said Darnay.

00:44:23.884 --> 00:44:26.856
Gabel spoke first.

00:44:26.916 --> 00:44:33.503
Charles Darnay did not want to be the Marquis Antebremand, he said.

00:44:33.563 --> 00:44:36.326
He did not want to be an aristocrat.

00:44:36.386 --> 00:44:39.797
He did not take any money from the people of France.

00:44:39.857 --> 00:44:42.418
He is a good man."

00:44:42.478 --> 00:44:46.149
Then Dr. Manette spoke.

00:44:46.209 --> 00:44:51.810
I was a prisoner in the Bastille for eighteen years, he said.

00:44:51.870 --> 00:44:54.441
The people in the courtroom cheered.

00:44:54.501 --> 00:44:57.052
Long live Dr. Manette!

00:44:57.112 --> 00:44:58.842
They shouted.

00:44:58.902 --> 00:45:01.793
Charles Darnay helped me.

00:45:01.853 --> 00:45:03.372
The doctor said.

00:45:03.432 --> 00:45:06.932
I was very sick, and he took care of me.

00:45:06.992 --> 00:45:09.062
He married my daughter.

00:45:09.122 --> 00:45:11.033
He is a good man.

00:45:11.093 --> 00:45:13.204
He came back to France.

00:45:13.264 --> 00:45:16.926
He wants to help Citizen Gabel.

00:45:16.986 --> 00:45:20.827
The people in the courtroom cheered again.

00:45:20.887 --> 00:45:23.198
Long live the Republic.

00:45:23.258 --> 00:45:25.819
Long live the people of France.

00:45:25.879 --> 00:45:27.520
They shouted.

00:45:27.580 --> 00:45:30.921
Charles Darnay was arrested in England.

00:45:30.981 --> 00:45:32.756
Dr Manette said.

00:45:32.816 --> 00:45:37.073
The English said, Darnay is a French spy.

00:45:37.133 --> 00:45:41.216
He is a friend of the revolutionaries in the American colonies.

00:45:41.276 --> 00:45:45.188
Now you say he is an enemy of France.

00:45:45.248 --> 00:45:47.228
You are wrong.

00:45:47.288 --> 00:45:49.770
Let him go.

00:45:49.830 --> 00:45:52.102
Shouted the people in the courtroom.

00:45:52.162 --> 00:45:55.023
He is a friend of the revolution.

00:45:55.083 --> 00:45:58.304
The judges made their decision.

00:45:58.364 --> 00:46:00.621
Not guilty.

00:46:00.681 --> 00:46:02.676
The President said.

00:46:02.736 --> 00:46:05.118
He spoke to Darnay.

00:46:05.178 --> 00:46:07.580
You are free!

00:46:07.640 --> 00:46:17.104
He said.

00:46:17.164 --> 00:46:33.680
Chapter 10 Citizen Bar Sad Charles Darnay stood outside the courtroom.

00:46:33.740 --> 00:46:35.461
He was free.

00:46:35.521 --> 00:46:37.522
He held Lucy in his arms.

00:46:37.542 --> 00:46:40.384
"'He is innocent.

00:46:40.444 --> 00:46:43.406
I have saved him,' said Doctor Manette.

00:46:43.426 --> 00:46:46.607
"'Let's go home now.'

00:46:46.668 --> 00:46:49.830
They returned to their rooms near the bank.

00:46:49.890 --> 00:46:53.972
Jerry Cruncher and Miss Pross went out to buy some wine.

00:46:54.032 --> 00:46:58.665
A little later the doctor was talking to Charles and Lucy.

00:46:58.726 --> 00:47:02.748
Suddenly, some revolutionary guards came into the room.

00:47:02.808 --> 00:47:06.100
One of the guards spoke to Charles.

00:47:06.160 --> 00:47:13.573
Citizen everymond, also called Darnay, you were under arrest, he said.

00:47:13.633 --> 00:47:16.314
Why is he under arrest?

00:47:16.374 --> 00:47:17.845
asked Dr. Manette.

00:47:17.905 --> 00:47:19.606
There was a trial.

00:47:19.666 --> 00:47:21.337
He is not guilty.

00:47:21.397 --> 00:47:23.658
He is free now.

00:47:23.718 --> 00:47:28.375
There will be another trial tomorrow, said the guard.

00:47:28.435 --> 00:47:30.830
What has he done wrong?"

00:47:30.890 --> 00:47:32.971
said Doctor Minette angrily.

00:47:33.031 --> 00:47:34.951
Who accuses him?

00:47:35.011 --> 00:47:37.432
You will know tomorrow.

00:47:37.492 --> 00:47:39.372
Said the guard.

00:47:39.432 --> 00:47:43.693
The guards took Darnay back to La Force Prison.

00:47:43.753 --> 00:47:45.754
Lucy cried.

00:47:45.814 --> 00:47:49.164
Her father held her in his arms.

00:47:49.225 --> 00:47:52.095
I have saved him once.

00:47:52.155 --> 00:47:54.136
Said Doctor Minette.

00:47:54.196 --> 00:47:56.594
I will save him again.

00:47:56.654 --> 00:48:01.014
I will speak at the trial tomorrow."

00:48:01.074 --> 00:48:07.116
Jerry Cruncher and Miss Pross were looking for some wine.

00:48:07.176 --> 00:48:11.356
They went into Ms. Surya Madam Defarge's wine shop.

00:48:11.417 --> 00:48:16.128
Miss Pross saw a man inside the shop.

00:48:16.188 --> 00:48:20.158
She cried out, "'Solarmen!

00:48:20.218 --> 00:48:22.309
What do you want?"

00:48:22.369 --> 00:48:24.530
said the man in English.

00:48:24.590 --> 00:48:26.487
He was angry.

00:48:26.547 --> 00:48:30.336
Solomon, said Miss Pross.

00:48:30.396 --> 00:48:33.489
You are my brother, Solomon.

00:48:33.550 --> 00:48:37.122
I've not seen you for many years.

00:48:37.183 --> 00:48:41.086
Be quiet, said the man.

00:48:41.146 --> 00:48:43.797
I have a different name now.

00:48:43.858 --> 00:48:46.529
I'm a revolutionary official.

00:48:46.590 --> 00:48:50.168
I'm an important man in the Republic.

00:48:50.228 --> 00:48:56.126
His name is Citizen Barsad, said another man.

00:48:56.187 --> 00:48:59.989
They all turned and looked at the person who had spoken.

00:49:00.050 --> 00:49:03.542
Darnay, said Barsad.

00:49:03.602 --> 00:49:05.784
Why are you here?

00:49:05.844 --> 00:49:10.487
No, I'm not Charles Darnay, said the man.

00:49:10.548 --> 00:49:13.100
My name is Sidney Carton.

00:49:13.160 --> 00:49:16.062
You saw me at the trial in London.

00:49:16.122 --> 00:49:19.244
My face is like Darnay's face.

00:49:19.304 --> 00:49:21.693
But I'm not Darnay.

00:49:21.753 --> 00:49:26.186
I want to see Darnay and his wife Lucy," Carton said.

00:49:26.246 --> 00:49:27.829
Where are they?

00:49:27.889 --> 00:49:32.336
Darnay is under arrest, said Bassad.

00:49:32.396 --> 00:49:35.049
He is in La Force prison.

00:49:35.109 --> 00:49:36.932
He will go to the guillotine.

